  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 105 PM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nThe primary concern with the forecast will the potential for\nmore frost development overnight. Opted to hold off on issuing\nanother Frost Advisory because low temperatures tonight will be\na few degrees warmer across the board, with most locations \nseeing overnight lows in the upper 30s to lower 40s. NBM \nensemble probabilities of temperatures falling below 37F are \nonly 10-20% for Monday morning, compared to 60-100% for this \nmorning. However, winds do look to become calm overnight, so \nisolated frost is possible in climatologically-favored cool \nspots that are low-lying and sheltered. Will message this risk \nin the HWO and forecast graphics. \n\nThe rest of the forecast period through next weekend looks to be\ntranquil. Increasing H5 ridging over the central and northern\nGreat Plains will drive a gradual warming trend in temperatures.\nTemperatures will be near typical mid-October values through\nTuesday. Afterwards, they will trend to around 8-12 degrees\nabove normal by the weekend. This would yield high temperatures\nin the upper 70s to lower 80s and overnight lows in the middle\nto upper 40s for next weekend.",
